## Plot Workpad

### Plan
- [ ] **Phase 1: Core Effect Pattern Migration**
  - [ ] Migrate services from  to 
  - [ ] Replace manual function wrappers with 
  - [ ] Convert custom errors to  pattern
  - [ ] Update all service layers to new patterns
- [ ] **Phase 2: Reactivity Layer Introduction**
  - [ ] Add Reactivity layer to core application
  - [ ] Introduce Atom/AtomRegistry for orchestrator state
  - [ ] Replace SubscriptionRef patterns with reactive Atoms
  - [ ] Add reactive state management to core services
- [ ] **Phase 3: Modern Client Architecture**
  - [ ] Add RcMap for resource-counted API clients
  - [ ] Implement ScopedRef for hot-swappable service instances
  - [ ] Add PersistedCache/Persistable for durable caching
  - [ ] Implement GitHub etag caching pattern from lalph
- [ ] **Phase 4: Enhanced Tracker Plugin Architecture**
  - [ ] Extract richer IssueSource trait from lalph patterns
  - [ ] Add preset routing and state enforcement
  - [ ] Add auto-merge label support
  - [ ] Enhance plugin context with reactive state
- [ ] **Phase 5: GitFlow Strategy Pattern**
  - [ ] Extract GitFlow as swappable strategy
  - [ ] Implement PR flow vs commit flow as Layers
  - [ ] Add merge conflict recovery
  - [ ] Add auto-merge capabilities
- [ ] **Phase 6: Advanced Features**
  - [ ] Add stall detection (no-output timeout)
  - [ ] Add task timeout → auto-decomposition
  - [ ] Add model routing by issue label
  - [ ] Add live task steering via streams
  - [ ] Add research agent phase

### Acceptance Criteria
- All current plot functionality preserved during migration
- New lalph patterns properly implemented and tested
- Architecture supports hot-swappable services and reactive state
- Enhanced tracker plugins with richer capabilities
- GitFlow strategies swappable via Layer configuration
- Advanced features (stall detection, auto-decomposition) functional
- All verification gates pass: typecheck + lint + test + build
- No breaking changes to plot CLI/TUI interfaces

